1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
All apps is the default. Add an app only when it needs different actions.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Choose Add app and select Safari.app. The editing scope now says Safari. Existing buttons inherit All apps.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Save for this app: lower-side click → Back. It works in Safari; other apps still use Desktop left.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,187
Advanced → App-specific settings lists the actions used by the selected app, including inherited defaults.

5
00:00:33,187 --> 00:00:40,187
Remove app deletes its GlideMouse setup, not the installed app. All apps defaults apply again.

6
00:00:40,187 --> 00:00:47,187
Undo restores the app setup. Choose Safari again from the scope dropdown to continue editing it.
